# Notices: readable text with inline actions

A notice the user should read (not logged in, read-only, unsaved draft, can't save) uses `UserNotice` from `@/components/common/UserNotice`:

- A leading ⚠️ (or another fitting emoji) and `text-foreground` text — never muted gray, since people need to read it.
- Actions are underlined words inside the sentence (`NoticeAction`), not separate boxed buttons.
- No bordered boxes with big buttons.

For logged-out states always use `LoginNotice` (`@/components/dependent/account/LoginNotice`): "⚠️ You're not logged in. **Log in** to {what it unlocks}." On phones it shortens itself to "**Log in** to {what it unlocks}." (no ⚠️).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="border rounded-lg p-3 text-muted-foreground">
  Log in to save your notes. <Button>Log in</Button>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<LoginNotice to="save your notes" />
```

Errors and warnings that aren't notices (validation, "couldn't save") stay bold yellow; see `warnings-bold-yellow.mdc`.
